📋 Development & Migration Guidelines
General Rules

Document everything in detail. Any code you write must be clearly documented.

Keep documentation consistent. If you make changes, update all relevant documentation to match.

Check codex_mistakes.md. Always review this file before making changes to avoid repeating known mistakes.

Never modify database files directly. Do not edit .db files or other binary artifacts. Only interact with databases via queries, migrations, or Python scripts.

Exclude database binaries from file change lists. Only list source code or migration scripts unless explicitly told otherwise.

Do not write to .md files. Documentation updates should only happen if specifically requested.

🔄 Migration Workflow
1. 🧱 Backup and Setup

Copy workout.db → backups/workout_<EPOCH>.db.bak

Copy workout.db → workout_new.db (this is the migration target)

Never work directly on workout.db

2. 📐 Define New Schema

Recreate the new schema manually in workout_new.db

Do not use CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS

Include all constraints and structural changes explicitly

Run PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF; before making schema changes

3. 🔁 Data Migration Logic

Use Python scripts to copy and transform data from workout.db → workout_new.db

Handle these cases carefully:

Relaxed constraint: Copy data as-is

Tightened constraint: Replace invalid/null values with fallbacks

Added column: Populate with default or computed values

Dropped column: Abort migration if any values exist

Merged/split tables: Implement custom transformation logic

Enum changes: Convert values to/from JSON or correct format

👉 Every step must log clearly (e.g., "Copied 200 rows from exercises")

4. 🔐 Foreign Key Safety

Keep PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF during migration

Re-enable only after all data is inserted

Then run PRAGMA foreign_key_check;

Abort migration if violations are found

5. ✅ Finalization

Do not create views or indexes during table migration

After successful migration:

Replace workout.db with workout_new.db

Keep the .bak backup safe

Print a clear success or failure message

🔥 Error Handling

Abort immediately on any exception

Do not attempt partial rollbacks of views or indexes

Recovery path = the .bak backup



DO NOT IN ANY ALTER ANY DB OR .MD FILES EVER!!! UNLESS EXPLICITLY ASKED
